  "body": "Follow-up to #287 (first slice: #382, the read-only Machines pane, merged).\n\n## What changed\n**Machines pane: create, edit and save `.mch` machine files.**\n- **New:** **New blank** (mill, lathe or mill-turn, starting from the keys that kind requires), **New from template** (copies the selected machine), and **Edit machine**.\n- **Property grid** with nine collapsible groups: General, Axes and travels, Rotaries and limits, Spindle range, Feeds, Tool changer and stations, Coolant codes, Live-tool codes, Units. Each field's tooltip names its key.\n- **Validation.** `machine::validate` (from #382) runs live.\n  - Each refusal is shown in red under its field. Refusals that belong to no field (for example a missing required axis) are listed above the grid.\n  - **Save and Save As are disabled while any refusal stands**, so a refused file is never written.\n- **Save / Save As.**\n  - Save asks \"Write <path>?\" before writing.\n  - Save As asks for a name in the user folder, and asks again before replacing an existing file.\n  - Closing with unsaved edits asks before discarding them.\n  - After a save the list is re-read and the new file is selected.\n- **Shipped machines are read-only.** A built-in machine, or a file under `assets/machines`, opens read-only, and Save on it opens Save As.\n- **Atomic write:** a temp file in the same folder, synced, then renamed.\n- **Unknown keys are kept.** Edits are made on the file's raw JSON, so keys the editor doesn't know survive a save.\n- **User folder:** `CAMCRAFT_MACHINES` (absolute paths only), otherwise `<platform data dir>/camcraft/machines`. Resolved in the app layer (`machine::store`), and the pane's list includes it.\n- **Not an undoable project edit.** Saving a machine *file* queues no command and adds nothing to the undo history, per the issue. Assigning a machine to a setup is #384.\n- **Code:** new app modules `machine/{store,fields,draft}.rs`; new UI `machine_file_editor.rs`. The existing Setup-pane `machine_editor.rs` is unchanged.\n- `docs/decisions/383-machines-edit.md`\n\n## How tested\n- App `machine_edit` (10 tests):\n  - round-trip keeping unknown keys;\n  - a refused file is not written, with refusals per field and refusals with no field;\n  - live-tool words all four or none;\n  - each blank kind;\n  - template and Save As, read-only shipped files, replace confirmation, bad names;\n  - the atomic write leaves no temp file;\n  - folder resolution with the override and for macOS, Windows and Linux (XDG);\n  - the catalogue lists the user folder;\n  - a bad field path is refused, not a panic.\n- App `machine_library` 11/11 and `machine` 32/32. These tests never read the tester's real machines folder.\n- UI `machines_` (7 tests, structural, no PNGs):\n  - a template takes new travels and codes and saves to the user folder;\n  - a backwards travel is refused on its field and nothing is written;\n  - editing a shipped machine saves as a copy;\n  - a hand-written user file keeps its unknown keys through an edit and save.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick`: app suites green. In ui, only the three headless-GPU tests fail (no adapter on this Mac), as on main.\n- `clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --tests -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Decisions to review\n- **Key order is not kept.** The workspace `serde_json` has no `preserve_order`, so a saved file's keys come out sorted; the content, unknown keys included, round-trips exactly. Turning `preserve_order` on would change every JSON writer in the workspace, project files included, so it's left for a separate issue.\n- **No coolant remove button yet.**\n\n## Not exercised (draft until the contributor's GUI check)\nA hands-on check in a release build. A test kit is prepared, sandboxed with `CAMCRAFT_MACHINES` so the real machines folder is untouched.\n\nChangelog: The Machines pane creates, edits and saves .mch machine files: new blank or from a template, a property grid with per-field validation that blocks the save, atomic writes to the user machines folder, unknown keys kept (#383)\n\nFixes #383\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
